`#[construct]` says a prop is read once while the instance is built, so the
instance carries no setter for it and a new value cannot be written in. The
answer is to build a new instance, and this page holds both places that do it.

Inside the factory, the recursive child sits in a reactive slot, and the slot
answers by reconciling: `__inst1_was_start[__inst1_i] === start` is what the
live instance was built from against what this render describes, and a
difference takes the else -- destroy, create, place.

At the bottom, `seeded(start=k, more=0)` sits at a position no render owns, and
the `bump` handler answers it directly: build from the new value, put the new
root in before the old one, take the old one out, destroy it, and rebind the
name. The new root goes in first because that is what keeps `after` after it --
InsertBefore is the operation, and the whole thing is gated on the platform
declaring it. fyne and gtk4 do not, and there this program is a positioned
build error naming the platform rather than a page that drops the write.

`__n1__pos` is why the position is bound at all: the anchor outlives the
instance it holds. `__n1` is `var` rather than `const` for the same reason.

deny out/none/html/index.html `__n1.__set_start` -- a construct prop has no setter; calling one is the emission this rebuild replaced
deny out/none/html/index.html `const __n1 = ` -- the rebuild assigns the name, so a const binding throws on the first click
deny out/none/html/index.html `data-sngl-id="__n1__` -- the roots the rebuild binds are its own locals, not page refs to look up: a querySelector for one renamed the local by collision

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:macro"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

component seeded(#[construct] start int, more = 0) node {
    var n = start
    button(text="bump inner", @click { n = n + 5 })
    text(value="s:" + string(n))
    if more > 0 {
        seeded(start=start, more=more - 1)
    }
}

component App() node {
    var k = 10
    text(value="before")
    button(text="bump", @click { k = k + 1 })
    seeded(start=k, more=0)
    text(value="after")
}

window(title="H", href="/index.html") {
    App()
}
